In <83774@hydra.gatech.EDU> gt0040a@prism.gatech.EDU (Tom Sorensen) writes:

>An Ogre Lord zapped a wand of striking at me and missed. I got the message:
>You are crushed by pieces of the drawbridge.
>(Or something similar).

>This is a bug- the drawbridge had already been lowered, so this should NOT
>have happened. I would be *REALLY* PO'd if I hadn't kept a copy of my SAV
>file in case of a system crash.

Sorry, I don't think that this is a bug.  Having been killed by
*exploding* drawbridges a couple of times now, I am fairly confident
that this is what happened to you.  The drawbridge seems to blow up if
you shoot certain wands at it, etc.  But it only does this (as far as I
can tell) *if it is already down*!

Being crushed by the descending drawbridge is a different death, with a
different message--the mention of "pieces" is your clue that the
drawbridge exploded, rather than descended (a 2nd time), to kill you.

This is a new game.  It is *descended* from 3.0, but it is *not* 3.0. 
Don't accuse it of having bugs simply because it doesn't always act
the same as 3.0.

If you're into playing an honest game, you'll quit now, and remove the
entry from the high score list.  You died an honest death, not a
bug-caused death.  Anyway, that's what I'd do, since I enjoy the
additional challenge of taking my lumps and starting over when the game
scores a clean kill on me.  (I also never *choose* a character class,
and I wish that there was a command-line option to tell it to assign me
a random character class without asking.)
